{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/y1s7epgv","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":64,"top":581,"width":1130,"height":49},"text":"Expected benefit: clearer preparation. User trials still need to measure it.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":25,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#576574","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/e0fm9a","slideIndex":2,"text":"R — Reason\nSpeaker: Raghav\nTarget: 35 seconds\n\nWe chose this problem because software can support a practical first step: recording the concern and preparing it for an advocate. The intended beneficiaries are people who prefer a familiar language or voice input, and advocates receiving a concise account. Our expected benefit is clearer preparation. We have not measured reduced effort or better legal outcomes. That distinction keeps our objective realistic. Siddharth will explain the scope.\n\nEvidence:\nC:/Users/DELL/Vakil-Setu/rebuild/docs/requirements.md\nC:/Users/DELL/Vakil-Setu/rebuild/docs/decisions.md"}
